  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "6cy9yvi3PVudt4UCoZftr7XP4m0=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:44:15.506Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The `analytics-engine` is described as \"a powerful, distributed, time-series analytics system, written in Typescript\", and its shape is a module split that mirrors the reactor's storage-agnostic design:\n\n- **`core/`** \u2014 the primary interface for interacting with the engine, and the home of the **query and aggregation** components;\n- **`knex/`, `pg/`, `browser/`** \u2014 the backing **storage engines**.\n\nSo the query surface is written once and the persistence is chosen per host: `pg` for a server, `browser` for an in-page store, `knex` for anything else it can reach. That is the same separation the reactor makes between `IOperationStore` and its Kysely implementation, and it is why the analytics hooks in reactor-browser can present the same query API a switchboard uses.\n\nToolchain notes for anyone working in it: `pnpm` as the package manager, `tsc-watch` as the filewatcher, `vitest` for tests, every module extending the root `tsconfig.json`, and the repository configured as a **pnpm workspace** so `pnpm install` at the root installs for every module and `pnpm test` runs every suite.\n\n## Provenance\n- `packages/analytics-engine/README.md` \u2014 Overview; Development Quickstart (module layout, tooling, workspace)\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:44:15.506Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:44:15.506Z"
    }
  },
